{
  "_about": [
    "The move pool table of Gielinor Go: the one place to read and tune what creatures can learn (issue 21).",
    "scripts/gen-moves.py reads this file and species.json and writes moves.json, which the plugin loads.",
    "A move: id, name, style, power (1.0 = a plain attack), accuracy (0.5 to 1.0), slot (ATTACK, or SECOND for a",
    "breath: it plays the species' second attack animation when it has one), icy (a breath shown with the icy",
    "projectile), effect (status + chance: POISON, VENOM, BURN, FREEZE or STUN, rolled after a hit; issue 22).",
    "A pool lists [move id, level it is learned at], levels rising. Every pool starts with a power 1.0, accuracy 1.0",
    "move at level 1, so early battles play as before. A creature knows at most 4; the newest 4 unlocked are what a",
    "wild creature of that level knows.",
    "A pool's styles say which species styles it fits; a species of another style gets the default pool of its own.",
    "Rules are tried in order and the first whose pattern (or names list) matches a species name picks its pool."
  ],
